          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            %em Deligne cohomology
            – or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Deligne
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Beilinson"} Beilinson
              cohomology
            – is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            that models
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+cohomology"} sheaf cohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+sheaf"} locally constant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaf
            (modeling
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            data.
          %p
            The
            %em Deligne complex
            is like a truncated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            but, crucially, with the sheaf of 0-forms – the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            \- replaced by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+group"} multiplicative group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^\times
            under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+map"} exponential map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo ×
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi log
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi d
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi n
                    %mo ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left[
                  \\mathcal{O}^\times
                  \\stackrel{d log}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\Omega^1
                  \\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\Omega^2
                  \\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\cdots
                  \\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\Omega^n
                  \\right]
                  \\,.
          %p
            Deligne cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi conn
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{n+1}_{conn}(X, \mathbb{Z})
            in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves+of+abelian+groups"} sheaves of abelian groups
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercohomology"}> hypercohomology
            ”).
          %p
            This was introduced in (
            %a{:href => "#Deligne71"}> Deligne 71, Section 2.2
            ) in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+geometry"} analytic geometry
            (hence using
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+differential+forms"} holomorphic differential forms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+filtration"} Hodge-filtered
            version of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beilinson+regulator"} Beilinson regulator
            from
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+cohomology"} motivic cohomology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Brylinski93"} Brylinski 93
          %p
            In smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            the typical minor variant has the sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi U
                    %mo ̲
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underline{U}(1) = C^\infty(-,U(1))
            of
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            in degree
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi log
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi d
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi n
                    %mo ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left[
                  C^\infty(-,U(1))
                  \\stackrel{d log}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\Omega^1
                  \\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\Omega^2
                  \\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\cdots
                  \\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\Omega^n
                  \\right]
                  \\,.
          %p
            Given any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-groupoid"} n-groupoid
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
            whose underlying
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-group"} circle (n-1)-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+infinity-bundle"} principal infinity-bundle
            is trivialized. Passing to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            implicitly corresponds to considering the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stackification"} infinity-stackification
            of this
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stackification"} infinity-stackification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-stack"} smooth infinity-stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}
            which is the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+infinity-stack"} moduli infinity-stack
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of maps (of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stacks"} infinity-stacks
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FSS10"} FSS 10
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi conn
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^{n+1}_{conn}(X,\mathbb{Z})
                  \\simeq
                  \\pi_0(X \to \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn})
                  \\,.
          %p
            In this way Deligne cohomology, or rather the collection of Deligne
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in the Deligne complex that defines it, is considerably richer than other models for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cheeger-Simons+differential+characters"} Cheeger-Simons differential characters
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+group"} cohomology group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+infinity-stack"} moduli n-stack
          %p
            Explicitly, computing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            with coefficients in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+complex"} Deligne complex
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cohomology
            gives that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{A}
            on some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is represented with respect to a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
