          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            In any context where these symbols make the evident sense, the Deligne complex of degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo ×
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi log
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^\times \stackrel{d log}{\to}\Omega^1 \stackrel{d}{\to} \Omega^2 \to \cdots \to \Omega^n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in this complex.
          %p
            More generally one considers any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi 𝒪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow \mathcal{O}
            into the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow \mathcal{O} \stackrel{d}{\to} \Omega^1 \to \cdots \to \Omega^n
          %p
            For definiteness we consider here in detail the Deligne complex in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            modeled on
